# k1 at M=N=K=256, block 32x32, grid 8x8: every lane of a warp reads the
# same A element (1 sector) and consecutive B and C elements (2). Nsight
# Compute on this launch: 1,050,624 load requests over 1,576,960
# sectors and 2,048 store requests over 4,096, exactly these rows times
# their counts. The guard `x < M && y < N` reads only with M and the grid
# bound; without them which threads run the loop is not known, and its
# footprint is a bound.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k1/k1.sm_80.ptx --bind 0:M=256 --bind 1:N=256 --bind 2:K=256 --launch 32,32,1 --grid 8,8,1 | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k1/k1.sm_80.ptx --bind 1:N=256 --bind 2:K=256 --launch 32,32,1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
CHECK: kernel hgemm_naive(int, int, int, float, __half const*, __half const*, float, __half*)
CHECK: 1_naive.cuh:16  ld.global.u16  global load 2 B  warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)       [512 * %tid.y + 16384 * %ctaid.y + 8 * k[1_naive.cuh:15] + param_4 - 8]   k[1_naive.cuh:15]: +8 B/iter
CHECK: 1_naive.cuh:16  ld.global.u16  global load 2 B  warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)    [2 * %tid.x + 64 * %ctaid.x + 2048 * k[1_naive.cuh:15] + param_5 - 2048]  k[1_naive.cuh:15]: +2048 B/iter
CHECK: global bytes per CTA over the loop's own blocks: requested 1048576 B, unique 32768 B, in sectors 786432–1048576 B
CHECK: accesses outside loops:
CHECK: 1_naive.cuh:18  ld.global.u16  global load 2 B   warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)    [2 * %tid.x + 512 * %tid.y + 64 * %ctaid.x + 16384 * %ctaid.y + param_7]
CHECK: 1_naive.cuh:18  st.global.u16  global store 2 B  warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)    [2 * %tid.x + 512 * %tid.y + 64 * %ctaid.x + 16384 * %ctaid.y + param_7]
FREE: global bytes per CTA over the loop's own blocks: requested <= 1048576 B, unique <= 32768 B, in sectors <= 786432–1048576 B
